  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Liver and onions is a quick pan-fry: calf's liver cooked in a very hot pan until just done on the outside while still pink within, then served with caramelised onions, bacon, and a sage butter. The whole thing takes less than 25 minutes. The critical rule is speed: liver goes from perfectly cooked to tough and grey in under a minute if you leave it too long."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "tone": "tip"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Ask the butcher to slice the liver thin, about 5 mm. Thin slices cook evenly in 90 seconds per side. Thicker pieces need longer and are harder to get right."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 2,
          "items": [
            {
